  "notes": "{野営|やえい} means camping outdoors, especially in a rugged or field setting. Composed of {野|や} (field/wild) + {営|えい} (camp/quarters).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {野営|やえい}{地|ち}: campsite\n- {野営|やえい}{場|じょう}: camping ground\n- {野営|やえい}{訓練|くんれん}: field camping training (military)\n- {野営|やえい}する: to camp outdoors\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- キャンプ: camping (casual, general-purpose — most common in everyday speech)\n- {露営|ろえい}: bivouacking (literary/military, sleeping outdoors without shelter)\n- {宿営|しゅくえい}: billeting, encampment (military lodging)\n\nREGISTER:\n{野営|やえい} has a more serious, rugged tone compared to the casual loanword キャンプ. It appears more often in scouting, military, and outdoor survival contexts. For recreational camping at a designated campground, キャンプ is more natural.",
